            r1_brief: `6 p.m. The last tutorial with Mercedes Royo before you open: Tell me what you sell, to whom, and what you are on paper. The idea: repairs of computers and phones for anyone; a monthly maintenance fee for small businesses (advisers, clinics, shops), the problem eleven of the twenty interviews named; websites and online shops to order; or copy the big repair chain's catalogue at a lower price. The legal form: a comunidad de bienes between the two of you; a limited company with €3,000 of capital, half each; a limited company with €1 of capital, as the 2022 reform allows; or start without registering until you see if it works, charging without invoices.`,
            r1_note: `Deliverable: the value proposition and the legal form. This round is scored on the year as projected today; everything you have not decided yet follows current practice.`,
            r1_title: `Round 1 — Monday 14 December 2026: the idea and the legal form`,
            r2_brief: `9 a.m. The first week is over and the money has to be decided. The investment: a street-level shop with a window and a €16,000 refurbishment; the minimum, with two good laptops, tools, licensed remote-support and invoicing software and a coworking desk at €180 a month, for €5,000; the same plus €9,000 of equipment to resell; or nothing, with your old laptops and unlicensed software. The financing: only your savings; savings and a five-year bank loan of €12,000 at 7.5% with personal guarantees; savings and a participative loan from a public programme for young entrepreneurs, €15,000 at 4% with a first year of interest only, open to companies and not to a comunidad de bienes; or €10,000 of credit cards and a quick consumer loan at 22%.`,
            r2_note: `Deliverable: the initial investment and how it is financed. Scored on the year as projected today.`,
            r2_title: `Round 2 — Monday 11 January 2027: the investment and the financing`,
            r3_brief: `9 a.m. The first quarter is closed and Tomás Lacasa, the adviser you met at a chamber of commerce workshop, shows you the numbers. The price from April: below the chains, 25% under the cost-based price; the price calculated from costs, the margin and the break-even; 25% above, premium; or the first month free and discounts for whoever asks. The fixed costs from April: hire a full-time technician, €2,500 a month with social security; keep the structure lean but pay for what protects it, an adviser, invoicing software and professional liability insurance, €110 a month more; nothing, keep doing the paperwork yourselves at night; or €900 a month of paid advertising.`,
            r3_note: `Deliverable: the price and the fixed-cost structure from April. Scored on the year as projected today.`,
            r3_title: `Round 3 — Monday 5 April 2027: the price and the fixed costs`,
            r4_brief: `9 a.m. Two pieces of news. Elena Bergua, director of Clínica Dental Valdejalón, wants Nodo Cierzo to run all the clinic's IT, including the server with the patients' records: €1,200 a month. And Asesoría Lanaja has not paid a 90-day-old invoice, while the third-quarter VAT return (form 303) is due on 20 October. The clinic: sign a data-processing contract (GDPR Article 28), with logged remote access and no copies; do the job without a contract and copy the database to a USB stick to work from home; turn the job down; or pass it to a freelance friend without telling the clinic. The cash: set VAT and withholdings aside every month in a separate account and claim the invoice citing the 60-day legal limit; file form 303 without paying it and pay when the client does; the partners stop drawing pay from September to November; or open a €6,000 credit line.`,
            r4_note: `Deliverable: the clinic's job and the cash plan. This round is scored on the year as it closes.`,
